*
* A Composer/npm for MultiValue: it talks to a registry over HTTP, resolves a
* package, downloads its release tar archive and installs it into an account,
* pulling in its dependencies first.  The only non-MV operations (download,
* untar, build/catalog, deploy) go through the MVPKGOS seam, so this one source
* runs on any MV system that ships an MVPKGOS — MVX builds + links the package
* (BUILD-PKG/LINK-PKG); UniData compiles + globally catalogs it and deploys
* per-account VOC verbs.  HTTP/JSON are MVX intrinsics; UniData reaches them as
* the cataloged seam functions.
*
* The verb is built on the cmd command framework: it declares its subcommands
* and dispatches to one handler subroutine each (MVPKG.INSTALL, MVPKG.INFO, …),
* which read the invocation sentence themselves.  mvx-lang/cmd is a REQUIRED
* dependency: a cut-down copy used to be bundled here under cmd's own names,
* which did not "override" anything -- it collided, and which copy a CALL bound
* was the order the directory was read (#158).  Whatever installs mvpkg fetches
* cmd; the one case that cannot is INIT, below.
*
* INIT is the account bootstrap: it lays down MVPKG.INC/PLATFORM.H, the store and
* lock pointers, and whatever else a fresh account needs — the very things the
* rest of the toolchain (cmd, getopt) relies on.  So it must run WITHOUT the cmd
* framework; hand-dispatch it here, ahead of CMD.
$IFDEF MVX
   BSENT = SENTENCE()
$ELSE
   BSENT = @SENTENCE
$ENDIF
   BVERB = OCONV(FIELD(BSENT, " ", 2), "MCU")
   IF BVERB = "INIT" THEN
      CALL MVPKG.INIT
      STOP
   END
   * AND INSTALL, WHILE cmd IS NOT HERE YET.  cmd is a required dependency, so
   * the very first thing a fresh account does is fetch it -- and it cannot ask
   * the command framework to dispatch the command that installs the command
   * framework.  Bundling a copy of cmd was the old answer and it collided with
   * the real package (#158); this is the same trick INIT already uses.
   *
   * ONLY while cmd is absent.  Once it is in the lock the normal path runs, so
   * `install --help` and the usage screen behave like every other subcommand.
   * MVPKG.INSTALL reads its own sentence (every handler does), so dispatching
   * it directly is the same call CMD.RUN would have made.
   * IS THE FRAMEWORK HERE?  Same probe HASGIT uses in MVPKG.INSTALL, for the
   * same reasons: the lock answers on every platform, and on MVX a LINKed or
   * system-account package is callable without being in this account's lock --
   * which is how a toolchain install arrives, so asking the lock alone would
   * refuse to run on a perfectly good install.  Probing rather than calling
   * also matters on jBASE, where an unresolved CALL traps into the debugger
   * instead of returning an error (mv_package#54).
   BHAVECMD = 0
   CALL MVPKG.HAS("mvx-lang/cmd", BHAVECMD)
$IFDEF MVX
   IF CATALOGED("CMD.INIT") THEN BHAVECMD = 1
$ENDIF
   IF NOT(BHAVECMD) THEN
      IF BVERB = "INSTALL" THEN
         CALL MVPKG.INSTALL
         STOP
      END
      * ANY OTHER COMMAND, WITH NO FRAMEWORK, IS A BOOTSTRAP THAT DID NOT
      * FINISH.  Without this the answer is a raw runtime error naming CMD.INIT,
      * which tells the operator nothing about what to do next.
      PRINT "mvpkg: the cmd package is not installed, so only these work here:"
      PRINT "  MVPKG init {<url>}              provision this account"
      PRINT "  MVPKG install mvx-lang/cmd      fetch the command framework"
      PRINT "Whatever installed mvpkg normally does the second one for you."
      STOP
   END
   CALL CMD.INIT("MVPKG", "MultiValue package manager")
   CALL CMD.ADD("INSTALL", "install a package (name); --source [<dir>] builds an editable working copy", "MVPKG.INSTALL")
   CALL CMD.ADD("INFO", "show a package's registry metadata (name)", "MVPKG.INFO")
   CALL CMD.ADD("LIST", "show installed (managed) packages", "MVPKG.LIST")
   CALL CMD.ADD("UPDATE", "upgrade installed packages to latest ({name})", "MVPKG.UPDATE")
   CALL CMD.ADD("REMOVE", "uninstall a package (name)", "MVPKG.REMOVE")
   CALL CMD.ADD("REGISTER", "adopt an already-installed package (name {version})", "MVPKG.REGISTER")
   CALL CMD.ADD("SEARCH", "find packages by name/description (term)", "MVPKG.SEARCH")
   CALL CMD.ADD("SETUP", "set the registry URL (url)", "MVPKG.SETUP")
   CALL CMD.ADD("CONFIG", "show or set config ({minimum-stability|prefer-stable} {value})", "MVPKG.CONFIG")
   CALL CMD.ADD("REBUILD", "rebuild the host's native library", "MVPKG.REBUILD")
   CALL CMD.ADD("INIT", "provision this account for package management ({url})", "MVPKG.INIT")
   CALL CMD.ADD("FIXPERMS", "hand MVPKG's files to the operator, or move to a new one ({user})", "MVPKG.FIXPERMS")
   CALL CMD.ADD("PERMS", "show or edit the vendor shell-command grant ({list|add|remove} {cmd})", "MVPKG.PERMS")
   CALL CMD.ADD("NOTIFY", "login-proc check: modal if a deployed package is behind the store", "MVPKG.NOTIFY")
   CALL CMD.RUN
